Technology and Cost Challenges Remain Important

Wafer manufacturers face demanding requirements for crystalline quality, surface uniformity, contamination control and production consistency. At the same time, customers seek competitive pricing and dependable delivery.

Building new production capacity requires capital investment, while qualifying new suppliers can take time. Concentration among established producers and the technical complexity of manufacturing create significant barriers to entry.

These factors make production efficiency, process innovation and customer relationships central to competition in the 12-inch wafer market.

